---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergencyStrip from '../components/EmergencyStrip.astro';

// Thin-stroke line icons (Lucide-derived paths, 1.5px stroke) — design rule 1: never emoji.
const icon = {
  video: 'M15.6 10.3l4.4-2.5v8.4l-4.4-2.5M4 6.8h9.6a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v6.4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8.8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z',
  home: 'M3 10.5L12 3l9 7.5M5.5 8.8V20h13V8.8M9.8 20v-6h4.4v6',
  clinic: 'M4 20V6.5L12 3l8 3.5V20M4 20h16M12 8v6M9 11h6',
  message: 'M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H4l1.7-3.4A8 8 0 1 1 21 12z',
  file: 'M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-5-5zM14 3v5h5M9 13h6M9 17h6',
  rx: 'M7 4h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H7V4zM7 11v9M10 13l7 7M17 13l-7 7',
};
---
<Base title="How it works — DuBose, M.D." active="how" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,88px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The mechanics</span>
          <h1>How it works</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          No packages, no tiers, no fine print. Here is the whole process,
          start to finish.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · Your first 90 days -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The experience</span>
          <h2>Your first 90 days</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="tl-item">
            <h3>Before anything: a free conversation</h3>
            <p>
              Thirty minutes by video. You tell me what&rsquo;s going on,
              and I tell you honestly whether I can help. If we both feel
              good about it, you join — $100 a month, cancel anytime. If
              not, no bill and no pressure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <h3>Week 1&ndash;2: I do my homework, then we meet properly</h3>
            <p>
              I request and actually read your records before your first
              visit — you shouldn&rsquo;t have to re-tell years of history
              from memory. Then your first full visit: up to 90 minutes,
              everything on the table — history, medications, concerns,
              goals. Longer, or split into two sittings, if your situation
              needs it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <h3>Week 2&ndash;4: we fill in the picture</h3>
            <p>
              Labs if we need them — I&rsquo;ll tell you the cash price
              before anything is drawn, or we&rsquo;ll use your insurance. An
              exam at your home or my clinic space if your situation calls
              for hands-on. Every result comes back explained, in plain
              words.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <h3>By about week 4: you have a plan</h3>
            <p>
              A short written plan in your portal: what we&rsquo;re working
              on, in what order, what I&rsquo;m doing, what you&rsquo;re
              doing, and when we check progress. A plan we both agreed
              to.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-item">
            <h3>Then: the rhythm that fits your situation</h3>
            <p>
              Some patients see me every two weeks while we work through
              something active. Some check in monthly, quarterly, or mostly
              message me between an annual deep review. There&rsquo;s no
              required schedule and no per-visit charge — and around 90 days,
              we look at how it&rsquo;s going.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Where care happens -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Care settings</span>
        <h2>Where care happens</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards c3">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.video} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>By video — most of the time</h4>
          <p>
            Unhurried video visits from wherever you are. Most primary
            care — follow-ups, results, medication changes, new concerns —
            works well this way when there is enough time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.home} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>At your home — when it matters</h4>
          <p>
            When an exam genuinely needs hands-on and home is the right
            place, I come to you. Scheduled ahead, within my service area, at
            no extra charge — it&rsquo;s part of how I practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.clinic} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>At my clinic space — when that&rsquo;s better</h4>
          <p>For exams and procedures better done in an equipped room.
          Scheduled as needed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:36px">
        Where each visit happens is a clinical judgment we make together —
        video for most things, in person when your body needs to be in the
        room. I don&rsquo;t run a big office, and you&rsquo;re not paying for
        one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Between visits -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Day to day</span>
        <h2>Between visits</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps c3">
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.message} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>Message me directly</h4>
          <p>
            A question, a symptom you&rsquo;re unsure about, a pharmacy
            problem — send it through the secure portal. I answer within
            1&ndash;2 business days, usually faster.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.file} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>Results, explained</h4>
          <p>
            Nothing sits unexplained in a portal. Every lab and report comes
            with my note: what it means, what we&rsquo;re doing about it, or
            why it&rsquo;s genuinely fine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <div class="icon-chip">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icon.rx} /></svg>
          </div>
          <h4>Refills, without games</h4>
          <p>
            Prescriptions are managed at visits so you&rsquo;re not
            chasing renewals. When something slips, message me and
            I&rsquo;ll sort it out.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Availability -->
  <section class="section" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Boundaries</span>
          <h2>When I&rsquo;m available, honestly</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I keep business hours, Monday through Friday. I don&rsquo;t
            promise 24/7 access, evenings, or weekends. One physician
            cannot be always on call and still practice well. The trade is
            simple: bounded hours, and real attention inside them.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also take real time away each year. You&rsquo;ll know in
            advance through the portal. I still check incoming results and
            messages for anything important — away means slower, never
            unaware. Refills and ongoing care are arranged before I go,
            and urgent needs follow the same rules as always:
          </p>
          <EmergencyStrip />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · What's in the price -->
  <section class="section tight band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
          <h2>What&rsquo;s in the price</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            All of the above is the membership: $100 a month, no per-visit
            charges, cancel anytime. Labs, medications, specialists, and
            hospitals are billed by those providers — usually through your
            insurance — and I help you navigate the costs.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a class="quiet" href="/pricing">The full pricing picture, including insurance, Medicare, and Medicaid &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Ready to see if this fits?</h2>
        <p>Thirty minutes, by video, free — and an honest answer.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
